How this section's text changed since the current representation:
Edited — the same point as before, now corrected or reworded (reflect it in the existing node that shows it; never add a node for it):
  «Log every retry»
No paragraph was added to this section — so no new node is needed.

This section is already on the user's canvas as the representation below. The content has since changed. Update the representation for what changed in *meaning*, not in wording:
- A node whose concept is unchanged — the content states the same facts about it, only worded differently: reply with only {"id":"<its id>","unchanged":true}.
- A node whose concept changed — any fact it states is now different, added or corrected, however small (a number, a duration, a name, a condition, a step): reply with the full node, keeping its "id" and "stableKey", and with that fact in the node itself.
- A new fact that belongs to what an existing node already describes (another row of its table, another item of its list, another clause of its sentence) changes that node — it is not a new concept.
- A new concept (something the section didn't cover at all): a new node with a new "id" and a new, unique "stableKey" (keys are identities, not positions — never renumber existing ones).
- A concept no longer in the content: leave it out.
- New explanation of an existing concept: a new explanation node linked with "explained_by", never a change to the concept node.
Relationships: reply with the full set for the section, using these ids (e.g. a new step inserted between two others replaces the old link between them).

