exports[`preserve prompts are byte-identical to before Knowledge Notes (G7) > the analysis patch, for every kind and for an unknown one > annotated 1`] = `
"You analyse one section of a document for a visual workspace: its main point and what it means, specific to its own content. You never invent facts the content doesn't contain, and you reply with JSON only.
----
A plan of one section, "Retries" (a "annotated" section: running prose where specific phrases or claims need their own explanation, caveat or source attached, without breaking the prose into cards), already exists, but it lacks takeaway and analysis. Do not redo the plan: give only what is missing, from the content below.

The plan's nodes:
- n1 (text): Retry

Then analyse it — the reader must understand it at a glance, not only find its details:
- "metadata.takeaway": the section's main point in one line of your own words (at most 15 words), e.g. "Merge v3 now; two decisions wait on the engineer". Always give one.
- What the annotations add that the prose alone wouldn't tell a reader — the one thing worth noticing across all of them.
- Put this analysis in "text" nodes marked "origin":"analysis" (e.g. {"id":"a1","type":"text","origin":"analysis","title":"Status","content":{"markdown":"..."}}), linked to what it is about where that helps. It may state what the content implies but doesn't say; it must never contradict the content or add facts it doesn't contain.
- The takeaway and analysis are specific to this content: name its own things (its checks, files, numbers, decisions). Never add a generic benefit or outcome it doesn't state ("improves user experience", "increases efficiency", "enhances reliability"); when the content gives no outcome, say what changed or what is open instead.
- The content's own details stay as they are above (in its own words, nothing left out). Analysis is added on top, never instead of them.

Reply with JSON only, exactly this shape:
